   "refusal_with_reason": "**Not a score decision at all.** A question the data cannot answer should retrieve the passage that says why with *high* similarity — that is the point of putting the limitations page in the corpus. So this type is measured by whether the reason chunk is in the top 5, and the answer is required to cite it; using \"low similarity\" as the test here would score a well-argued refusal as a failure.",
   "measured": "The first build made exactly that mistake: one score threshold was applied to both kinds of refusal and reported 0 of 2 reason-bearing questions as \"refused\" while the reason chunk was ranked first. The two rules are separate because the two questions are different questions."
